          guide: { why: "The plan asks to assess each measure on impact, effort and risk. The plan prints no figure, so all three are the learner's own judgement and are never marked. The conditions to weigh against: a limited budget, time pressure, many existing content items.", lookFor: ["All three measures are assessed, not only the favourite.", "Each is judged on impact, effort and risk in the same terms.", "A judgement is tied to a condition (budget, time, content)."], pitfalls: ["Only the first measure is assessed in detail.", "A rating with no reason (“A is better”)."] },
